{"id":"n2-089","title":"～てまで (〜te made)","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Express the extent someone goes in order to achieve something; 'to the point of', 'even', 'so far as to'.","longExplanation":"The ～てまで grammar point is used to convey the extent someone goes to achieve something, highlighting the action one takes or the sacrifice one makes for a certain purpose. It can be translated as 'to the point of', 'even', or 'so far as to' in English. It is used with verbs, not adjectives or nouns.","formation":"Verb-て form + まで","examples":[{"jp":"彼は試験に合格するために、徹夜してまで勉強しました。","romaji":"Kare wa shiken ni gōkaku suru tame ni, tetsuya shite made benkyō shimashita.","en":"He studied to the point of staying up all night in order to pass the exam.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"試験","vocabId":"1312350","reading":"しけん"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"合格","vocabId":"1284600","reading":"ごうかく"},{"surface":"する","vocabId":"1595910","reading":"する"},{"surface":"ため","vocabId":"1157080","reading":"ため"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"徹夜","vocabId":"1437700","reading":"てつや"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"まで","vocabId":null},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[12]},{"jp":"この商品がほしかったので、朝早く起きてまで並んで買いました。","romaji":"Kono shōhin ga hoshikatta node, asa hayaku okite made narande kaimashita.","en":"I wanted this product so much that I went so far as to get up early and wait in line to buy it.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"商品","vocabId":"1347310","reading":"しょうひん"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ほしかっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ほしい"},{"surface